{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And the officers of the hosts shall appoint.</b> From the root of appointment and enumeration, that is, they shall appoint officers of the hosts at the head of the people to lead them, for the Torah commands in the way of customary conduct and performs miracles in hidden fashion. Now these things — the house, the vineyard, and the wife — are the desire of human beings, and they are a cause to draw the heart and make the thought preoccupied with them, so that those going out to battle have not a single heart in the battle but rather in his house or in his vineyard or in his wife; therefore the Torah commands that they return to their homes, for there is no benefit in them for those going out to battle but only great harm." "<b>And if</b> you gain insight into the parashah further, you will find in it a hidden matter, for the house, the vineyard, and the wife are allusions to the structure of the letters of the special Name and its plantings, and the meaning of the verse 'who is the man who has built' — the house of the Name — 'and has not dedicated it' to unify it as fitting and not to separate it, 'let him go and return to his house,' lest the attribute of Judgment strike him in battle, and another man come and wrap himself in his tallit and dedicate the house of HaShem. And so the vineyard with its plantings 'that he has not profaned' — rather, he made the holiness of below equal to that of above; and so the betrothed wife 'to Israel, that he has not taken' — that is, that he did not attach above but rather separated. And they further added: 'who is the man who is fearful and faint of heart' — from the transgressions in his hand." "<b>Now,</b> the priest anointed with the anointing oil — the anointing was in the manner of a crown (נזר) or in the manner of a כ\"י, after he warned Israel concerning the crown and diadem upon his head, in the manner of what is said (Numbers 6:7): ״כי נזר אלהיו על ראשו״, and he specified for them the matter of the emanation (אצילות) from beginning to end, for from there comes the influence to the princes of above and to the hosts of the heavens, which are the stars and the constellations; all the princes and all the hosts of the constellations would attend to their affairs and grant them aid according to the influence coming from the Most High, and this is what is said: 'and the officers of the hosts shall appoint at the head of the people,' that is, that then the appointees — who are princes over the hosts of the constellations — would go at the head of the people to carry out their action and make their enumerations and pour forth the influence coming to them from above for the benefit of Israel and for their glory."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {2 "The abbreviation כ\"י appears in the Hebrew; left unresolved as it stands, possibly 'כתר ישראל' or similar but not expandable with confidence from context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:47.210104005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}